Title: pandoc citations
Bibliography: refs.bib
Bibliography mode: replace
Bibliography style: chicago
Resolve citations: true
Pandoc citations: true
------------------------------------

In-text @Quine:1948 and with a locator @Quine:1948 [p. 33].

Parenthetical [@Quine:1948], with a locator [@Quine:1948, p. 33], with a prefix
[see @Quine:1948, p. 33], author suppressed [-@Quine:1948], and in text -@Quine:1948.

Several at once [@Quine:1948; @Skyrms:1996], and a group whose prefix and suffix
sit where natbib can hold them [see @Quine:1948; @Skyrms:1996, pp. 3-5].

A braced key @{Quine:1948} and [@{Skyrms:1996}, chap. 2].

A group with per-item locators has no natbib equivalent, so it is left exactly as
written and warns: [see @Quine:1948, p. 1; also @Skyrms:1996, p. 2]

Directives keep their names: @span[a directive]{.k}, not a citation key. A link
[text](http://example.com), an address me@example.com and an escaped \@word are
untouched, and natbib \citep[cf.][p. 9]{Quine:1948} still works.

@bibliography{title="References"}
